From 7a5b625d976e833ca1d7bbc660d89b3e0dcb6e33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 17:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] extcon: sm5502: resolve coalesced attach/detach from the
 hardware state

sm5502_muic_irq_work() acts on the irq_attach and irq_detach flags in
sequence.  When both are set in the same run of the work item, which
happens whenever an attach and a detach interrupt are serviced in the
same batch, the attach handler publishes the correct cable state and the
detach handler immediately clears it again.

The result is a MUIC that reports no cable while one is plugged in.  On a
Galaxy Tab A (SM-T580) this leaves DEV_TYPE1 reading 0x20 (USB SDP) while
the extcon device reports USB=0 SDP=0 DCP=0, so a charger driver
consuming the extcon notifier falls back to its most conservative input
current limit and the battery discharges on a connected cable.  The state
only recovers on the next cable cycle.

The driver already knows how to determine the real state:
sm5502_muic_get_cable_type() reads ADC and DEV_TYPE1 and returns -EINVAL
when no cable can be identified.  Ask the hardware instead of replaying
both flags, so a coalesced pair resolves to whatever is actually plugged
in.  A genuine attach and a genuine detach behave as before.
---
 drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c | 21 +++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c b/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c
index c8c4b9ef72..9ceedb64d0 100644
--- a/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c
+++ b/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c
@@ -531,13 +531,22 @@ static void sm5502_muic_irq_work(struct work_struct *work)
 
 	mutex_lock(&info->mutex);
 
-	/* Detect attached or detached cables */
-	if (info->irq_attach) {
-		ret = sm5502_muic_cable_handler(info, true);
+	/*
+	 * Detect attached or detached cables.
+	 *
+	 * Both flags can be set in the same run, in which case replaying
+	 * them in order would leave the state of whichever came last.
+	 * Read the current cable type instead: a negative return means
+	 * nothing identifiable is connected.
+	 */
+	if (info->irq_attach || info->irq_detach) {
+		bool attached;
+
+		attached = sm5502_muic_get_cable_type(info) >= 0;
+
+		ret = sm5502_muic_cable_handler(info, attached);
+
 		info->irq_attach = false;
-	}
-	if (info->irq_detach) {
-		ret = sm5502_muic_cable_handler(info, false);
 		info->irq_detach = false;
 	}
 
